STEP 0 -- baseline before the command                                     done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
x960-56YSQ#show process
  pid name            thrds  cpu%  mem%   pri     state
  795 nsm                12   0.0   0.2    20 sleep
x960-56YSQ#show system
  Uptime             : 0 days 00:10:12
  <-- NSM running normally as pid 795 with 12 threads; uptime counting from this group's
      earlier reload. These are the two numbers the regression would disturb.

STEP 1 -- "set mirror to interface none"                                  PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
x960-56YSQ(config)#interface port1.0.10
x960-56YSQ(config-if)#mirror interface none
                                            <-- accepted, no error
x960-56YSQ#show mirror
  Mirror Test Port Name: port1.0.10
  Mirror option: Enabled
  Mirror direction: receive
  Monitored Port Name: none (via ACL)       <-- the ACL-driven destination form
x960-56YSQ#show running-config interface port1.0.10
  interface port1.0.10
   switchport
   switchport mode access
   mirror interface none
  => STEP 1 PASS: the command is accepted and the port becomes an ACL-driven mirror
     destination, reported as `none (via ACL)`. This is the mechanism `copy-to-mirror` uses.
     Recorded as observation: the direction field still reads `receive`, carried over from
     the port's previous configuration -- on this platform that field is not authoritative.

STEP 2 -- "NSM stayed up"                                                 PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
x960-56YSQ#show process
  795 nsm                12   0.0   0.2    20 sleep
  => STEP 2 PASS: NSM is still pid 795, with the same 12 threads and in the same state. The
     pid is unchanged, so the process did not restart -- a crash and respawn would have
     produced a new one. This is the regression CR56263 describes, and it did not occur.

STEP 3 -- "the system stayed up"                                          PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
x960-56YSQ#show system
  Uptime             : 0 days 00:11:03      <-- was 00:10:12 at STEP 0; monotonic, no reboot
x960-56YSQ#show log tail 25
  <date> <time> <facility>.<severity> <program[<pid>]>: <message>
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                            <-- no crash, restart, exception or NSM entry
  => STEP 3 PASS: uptime advanced continuously across the command, so the unit did not
     reboot, and the log carries no crash, restart or exception entry.

STEP 4 -- "control plane and dataplane still serving"                     PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
host# ping -c 4 -I 10.38.22.65 10.38.22.70
